# The pre-auth walled garden: the ONLY hosts an unregistered device may reach.
#
# Deliberately not in allow.d/ -- these must resolve for everyone but be
# reachable only by devices that have not registered yet. A registered student
# is blocked from them, which is the point: www.google.com is Google search.
#
# Google's device flow is what makes this list necessary. It needs no redirect
# URI, which matters because Google refuses private-IP redirect targets, so a
# portal at 192.168.63.1 could never be one. The cost is that the code is
# entered at www.google.com/device.
accounts.google.com
www.google.com

# NOT the google.com apex. It was tried, and the query log showed exactly what
# suffix matching admits to a not-yet-registered device: mail.google.com,
# chat.google.com and play.google.com all resolved. Google Chat is a chat
# client, which integrity-policy.md bans during a session, so the apex costs
# more than the dead end it fixes.
#
# The portal therefore names the host explicitly -- https://www.google.com/device
# -- and a student can always approve the code from a phone instead, which is
# the reliable path when a laptop browser misbehaves.
www.gstatic.com
ssl.gstatic.com
